  "content_description": "Action Item - Teams",
  "content_text_body": "When teams take risks and experiment, they learn how to be flexible, creative, and innovative. They may make mistakes, but they learn from them in ways that help them grow and improve. \n\n### Practice experimenting \n\nExperimenting involves making very small changes in standard processes. To learn how to experiment, try this [Team Experimentation Exercise](Team_Experimentation_Exercise). Pick one or two things to experiment with that you think will improve your regular meetings.\n\n### Identify opportunities for experimentation\n\nAs a group, write out a list of processes or regular tasks that could be improved. Note how each process could be improved. As a group, decide on which processes the team would like to experiment with. See if you can run ten small experiments in the next quarter.",
